    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Seiya Suzuki** (75.03) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92) leading the charge as our most efficient starts. **Seiya Suzuki** benefits from a rare intersection of favorable park factors and elite historical BvP data against Lodolo, while **Vinnie Pasquantino** is perfectly positioned in the lineup to exploit the home park advantage and a manageable matchup against Kyle Bradish. Furthermore, **Mickey Moniak** (72.51) remains a high-floor play today; his aggressive platoon advantage against Mahle drives his projection into elite territory, providing us the offensive production we need in a 5x5 Roto format.\n\nWhile the core of our lineup is set, the bench optimization for **Josh Naylor** (52.95) was the most difficult decision of the morning. **Josh Naylor** posted a respectable score, but he was ultimately edged out by the superior efficiency metrics of **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Austin Riley**, both of whom are projected to offer higher output relative to their slotting. We are proceeding with caution regarding the potential for weather interference; **Edwin Arroyo** and **Seiya Suzuki** are currently flagged with a 39% rain risk, which could force an in-game shuffle if conditions deteriorate. Additionally, while **Corbin Carroll** is a cornerstone of our stolen base strategy, owners should note that he is facing a tough task against Yoshinobu Yamamoto, whose elite hold skill (58% SB prevention) mitigates **Corbin Carroll**'s high-end speed potential. We will monitor the lineup postings for **Dalton Rushing**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Alex Freeland**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Austin Riley**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Corbin Carroll**, and **Vinnie Pasquantino** to ensure these projected order spots hold firm as we push for Roto gains.",
